      "patch": "@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n \n | Status    | Final      |\n | ---:      | :---       |\n-| Version   | 4.3.0      |\n+| Version   | 4.2.1      |\n | Approved  | 2026-10-14 |\n | Effective | 2026-10-20 |\n \n@@ -696,7 +696,7 @@ This section tracks significant revisions. Minor revisions, typographical change\n |         |            | Added 5.1.7.1, temporarily allow missing type or cause of Vulnerability |\n |         |            | Added Revision History section |\n |         |            | Changed Typographical fixes and re-numbering |\n-| <a name=\"history-4.3.0\"></a>4.3.0  | 2026-mm-dd | Complete changes from 4.2.0 |\n-|         |            | Changed 4.2.6, require CVE ID assignment for separate Vulnerabilities |\n-|         |            | Changed 4.2.11, require CVE ID assignment for Independently Fixable Vulnerabilities |\n-|         |            | Changed 4.1, note different vulnerability determination knowledge and outcomes between Supplier and other types of CNAs |\n+| <a name=\"history-4.2.1\"></a>4.2.1  | 2026-10-14 | Complete changes from 4.2.0 |\n+|         |            | Section 4.1, Vulnerability Determination was updated to add the following to the third paragraph: “Vulnerability determination at a Supplier CNA may have different outcomes than vulnerability determination at other types of CNAs, for example, because the latter does not have access to internal Product, engineering, and other information. See the CVE Program Glossary for definitions of relevant Program roles and terms.” |\n+|         |            | In Section 4.2.6, the word SHOULD was changed to MUST in: “CNAs MUST assign different CVE IDs to separate Vulnerabilities, as determined using the guidance in 4.1.” |\n+|         |            | In Section 4.2.11, the word SHOULD was changed to MUST in: “CNAs MUST assign different CVE IDs to different, Independently Fixable Vulnerabilities.” |"
